# arr[idx] = val through a plain pointer: address = arr + idx*2, the value
# preserved across `tax` with pha/pla, stored with sta.l $0000,x (ported
# from opensnes-emu test_indirect_store_acache; its pre-A6 frameless
# assertions no longer apply, see that file's note). The load of the
# address after pha reads 2 bytes above where it was stored.
in array_write: present lda(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)\n\tasl a\n\tsta(?: |\.b tcc__lf\+)(\d+)(?:,s)?\n\tlda(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)\n\tclc\n\tadc(?: |\.b tcc__lf\+)\1(?:,s)?\n\tsta(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)
# Re-pinned 2026-10-08: a store through a pointer loads X first, then the
# value (`tax` / `lda` / `sta.l $00NNNN,x`); no pha / pla around it.
# (offsets moved again on 2026-10-08: parameters are read in place and a
# value that never touches the stack gets no slot)
in array_write: present tax\n\tlda(?: \d+,s|\.b tcc__lf\+\d+)\n\tsta\.l \$000000,x
in array_write: absent pha
